  "final_text": "**Proposed disposition:** CLOSE_FP, with confidence 0.80. This is a proposal only, and a human analyst makes the decision.\n\n**Three facts that drove it:**\n1. The large BUY ICEBERG order O-00030261 (21,768, which is 8.97x depth) was executing before the only opposite-side trade. 5,835 (26.8%) filled in regular clips of about 816, against 544 on the opposite side. That supports genuine execution of the resting order, so feature (a) is absent.\n2. The only SELL trade (544) was under a different parent order, C-T-X1005-05-B, so under the closure standard it is a different client's order for an agency trader. The price moved +3 ticks, but reversion was 0, so feature (b) is not shown. An iceberg also hides its size, so it could not have signalled false size.\n3. There is no risk event, no public event, and no prior alerts. The trader is an agency desk with no registered market-making instruments, so market making is ruled out. There is no repetition in the session.\n\n**What would change my mind:** Evidence that the SELL under parent C-T-X1005-05-B was the same client's position as the BUY. A repeated cycle in other sessions would also change it.",
